---
// How to install the VS Code extension's beta, at the top of the VS Code page on
// beta.squiffystory.com only. The Marketplace doesn't take prerelease versions, so a beta's .vsix is
// only on its GitHub Release (vscode-publish.yml). squiffystory.com documents the stable release,
// which is on the Marketplace, so it doesn't show this. See "Deployments" in CLAUDE.md.
import { Aside } from "@astrojs/starlight/components";
import { betaSite } from "../channel.mjs";
---

{
	betaSite && (
		<Aside type="tip" title="Trying the beta">
			<p>
				These docs are for the next version of Squiffy. The VS Code Marketplace only has stable
				releases, so to try the beta of the extension, install it from a file:
			</p>
			<ol>
				<li>
					Go to the <a href="https://github.com/textadventures/squiffy/releases">releases on GitHub</a>,
					find the newest one marked "Pre-release", and download the <code>.vsix</code> file under{" "}
					<strong>Assets</strong>, named <code>squiffy-</code> and the version.
				</li>
				<li>
					In VS Code, open the Command Palette (<kbd>Ctrl+Shift+P</kbd>, or <kbd>Cmd+Shift+P</kbd> on
					a Mac), choose <strong>Extensions: Install from VSIX...</strong>, and pick the file. Or drag
					the file onto the Extensions view.
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p>
				A beta doesn't update itself. To get the next one, install its <code>.vsix</code> the same
				way, and it replaces the one you have. Use VS Code on the desktop to try a beta.
				Please <a href="https://github.com/textadventures/squiffy/issues">report any problems</a> on
				GitHub, with your VS Code version (<strong>Help &gt; About</strong>) and the extension's.
			</p>
		</Aside>
	)
}
